# Chronic pain trials on ClinicalTrials.gov, {P[start_year_min]}–{P[start_year_max]}

**The question.** Which interventional trials in five chronic pain conditions started between {P[start_min]} and {P[start_max]}, who runs them, why do they stop, are results posted, and do outcomes cover the IMMPACT core domains (an expert consensus on what pain trials should measure)?

**Data and method**
- ClinicalTrials.gov API v2 (version {N[api_version]}), pulled {N[pull_date]} (registry data dated {N[data_date]}): {N[n_queries]} searches, {N[pulled_unique]:,} unique trials.
- Keyword rules on registry text kept {N[included]:,} trials in {P[n_groups]} groups, excluding headache, cancer pain and acute postoperative pain.
- Percentages are of all {N[included]:,} trials unless stated; every number comes from `outputs/numbers.json`.

**Five key findings**
- **Musculoskeletal pain dominates.** Chronic low back and other musculoskeletal pain makes up {D[pct_msk]}% ({N[by_group][MSK]:,}); complex regional pain syndrome only {N[by_group][CRPS]}; chronic postsurgical pain {T[cpsp_any]}, of which {T[cpsp_prevention]} are prevention studies. Starts rose from {T[starts_first_year]} in {P[start_year_min]} to {T[starts_last_year]} in {P[start_year_max]}, including planned starts ([figure](fig1_trials_per_year.png)).
- **Mostly small, academic, non-drug trials.** Only {T[pct_drug]}% list a drug or biological; the rest test devices, procedures, exercise or psychological care. Universities, hospitals or non-profits lead {D[pct_other_sponsor]}%, industry {D[pct_industry]}%. Median planned or actual enrolment is {T[enrol_median]} (interquartile range, the middle half: {T[enrol_q1]}–{T[enrol_q3]}).
- **Low accrual is the commonest stated reason to stop.** Of {T[tw_n]} trials stopped early ({T[tw_terminated]} terminated after enrolment began, {T[tw_withdrawn]} withdrawn before it), {T[tw_low_accrual]} ({T[tw_low_accrual_pct]}%) cite low accrual (too few recruits), {T[tw_funding]} ({T[tw_funding_pct]}%) funding and {T[tw_covid]} ({T[tw_covid_pct]}%) COVID-19; reasons as stated, sorted by keyword rules ([figure](fig2_stop_reasons.png)).
- **Results are rarely posted.** Of {R[eligible]:,} completed or terminated trials with primary completion at least {P[results_lag_months]} months before the pull, {R[pct]}% have results posted: {T[results_pct_industry]}% of {T[results_n_industry]} industry-led and {T[results_pct_other]}% of {T[results_n_other]:,} academic-led trials. Not a compliance rate: the legal duty covers only some trials.
- **Primary outcomes centre on pain intensity.** {T[immpact_pain_pct]}% of trials have a pain-intensity primary outcome and {T[immpact_physical_pct]}% physical functioning, but only {T[immpact_emotional_pct]}% emotional functioning and {T[immpact_global_pct]}% participant ratings of improvement or satisfaction. Of {T[immpact_n_measures]:,} primary outcome measures, {I[measures_none_pct]}% fit no IMMPACT domain (e.g. opioid use).

**HK/Asia.** {A[n]} trials ({A[pct_of_included]}%) have a site in the nine Asian places in scope, led by mainland China ({T[asia_china]}), South Korea ({T[asia_korea]}) and Taiwan ({T[asia_taiwan]}). Hong Kong has {H[n]}: {T[hk_msk]} musculoskeletal, {T[hk_cpsp]} postsurgical; {T[hk_academic]} academic-led (PolyU {T[hk_polyu]}, HKU {T[hk_hku]}, CUHK {T[hk_cuhk]}). Compared with {T[non_asia_n]:,} trials sited only outside Asia, they are larger (median enrolment {T[asia_enrol_median]} vs {T[non_asia_enrol_median]}) and more often industry-led ({A[pct_industry]}% vs {T[non_asia_pct_industry]}%).

**Limitations.** Registry data only (publications not checked); many mainland Chinese trials register only on ChiCTR, so China is under-counted; inconsistent coding means keyword rules misclassify some trials; fields are self-reported and often stale ({D[pct_unknown_status]}% have "unknown" status); data are as of {N[pull_date]}.

**Next steps.** Add ChiCTR and WHO registry data; hand-check a random sample to measure rule accuracy; link trials to publications.
